<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Icons.axaml - one StreamGeometry per icon, keyed by purpose.

    Source: Fluent UI System Icons (MIT License, (c) Microsoft Corporation),
    https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-system-icons - the 20px "regular" SVG path data,
    copied verbatim (viewBox 0 0 20 20). Use via PathIcon: <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource Icon.Volume}"/>.

    Replaces the Segoe Fluent Icons glyphs used by the WinUI app:
      E703 Icon.Connection   (Connection Type card, Connection nav item)
      E70D Icon.ChevronDown  (expander, expanded)
      E76C Icon.ChevronRight (expander, collapsed)
      E72C Icon.Refresh      (refresh COM ports button)
      E767 Icon.Volume       (volume OSD)
      E7F3 Icon.Speaker      (Device 1/2 cards, Output Devices nav item)
      EBE8 Icon.Debug        (Debug Logging card)
    New: Icon.Muted (OSD), Icon.Sliders / Icon.Buttons / Icon.Settings (nav items).
    Icon.Device.* (one per ScreenIcon, see the comment above them).
    Drawn for Volco (not Fluent): Icon.Speaker (a loudspeaker, for output-device switches, so it
    no longer duplicates Icon.Volume), Icon.Grip, Icon.More, Icon.Plus, Icon.Mode,
    Icon.Status.* (StatusLine), Icon.Close (the snackbar), Icon.Pencil / Icon.Check (the mode
    tabs' edit button and its Done state).
-->
